# Call-site ledger of tabulate at 3b4cd509820e4c45cd2aaba833aa585ea6308b94.
#
# The scope rules A, B1-B5 and C are in macro-benchmark/README.md; tabulate.md
# shows how this ledger applies them and records every judgement. The package
# is one module. Its public names are tabulate(), simple_separated_format(),
# the names Line, DataRow, TableFormat, the class JupyterHTMLStr (which
# tabulate() returns for html, with its public property str) and the module
# flags; everything else has an underscore. A table cell, a header and
# every other argument of tabulate() is a client object: opaque (B5) unless
# the package checks its class with isinstance or type() before the call, or
# the documentation fixes its type (B4: a dict of iterables, a list of dicts
# or OrderedDicts, a dict of headers, str format specifications). The cells
# that tabulate() hands to the private helpers after _format are str.
default reject tabulate.JupyterHTMLStr.str: the name str at this site is the builtin str (called, or passed to isinstance or map); the property JupyterHTMLStr.str runs only on an attribute load .str of a JupyterHTMLStr, and the package never loads that attribute

